## Checklist for New Scratch Orgs

Before creating a scratch org, ensure:

- [ ] Dev Hub org has Data Cloud licenses
- [ ] Salesforce CLI is installed and up to date
- [ ] Authenticated to Dev Hub org
- [ ] Scratch org definition file includes `Einstein1AIPlatform` feature
- [ ] `enableEinsteinGptPlatform` is set to `true`
- [ ] `enableAgentPlatform` is set to `true`
- [ ] Edition is set to `Developer` or `Enterprise`
- [ ] Appropriate duration days configured (max 30)
- [ ] Descriptive alias provided for easy identification

## Quick Start Command

For quick scratch org creation with Agentforce and Data Cloud:

```bash
# One-line command to create and open
sf org create scratch -f config/project-scratch-def.json -a agentforce-dev -d 30 -s && sf org open
```

This ensures every scratch org created in your project is ready for Agentforce agent development, Prompt Builder, Model Builder, and Data Cloud integration.
